{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-pm-exhaust-runspec",
    "description": "PENDING (PLAN.md 7.5 step 7d). The `process-pm-exhaust` RunSpec -- seven PM pollutant-processes, 728 rows, 104 cohorts on every block. It does NOT reproduce yet. When it was first measured (2026-09-22) it was not only short: of the 456 rows this chain emitted, 37 were right. Two of the three causes are now fixed, and the chain emits 248 rows of which 104 -- every EC cell -- are right and none is spuriously claimed. `n_outputRate` is bound to what the chain computes (248) so the document runs.\n\nTHE CYCLE IS NOT THE GAP. `runspecchainedto` has 11801 -> 11501 -> 11801 and 11801 -> 11901 -> 11801, and docs/process-pm-exhaust.md 2.8 already says why that does not matter: the table records `SulfatePMCalculator`'s INPUTS, and the arithmetic under it is a DAG. `fixtures/process-pm-exhaust.esm` computes it on the snapshot path, 728 of 728 cells at 7.516e-06. So this rung is moving machinery that exists into onroad/model.esm, not inventing it.\n\nWHAT IT WAITS ON, MEASURED 2026-09-22 against the run's own MOVESOutput, per block:\n\n* EC (112) -- DONE: 104 of 104 at 5.272e-06. Every wrong cell had been off by exactly `1/generalFuelRatio` on 11201 (1/1.0909107 on gasoline and E85 from 2001, 1/0.9727 on diesel through 2006): BaseRateCalculator multiplies a rated pollutant-process by the `generalFuelRatio` rows no other calculator moves away, and the model had no such factor. It is `rt_baseFuelRatio` now, forms A and B of the existing templates. Still 20 extra electricity rows, rated at exactly zero, which MOVES drops because `SulfatePMCalculator` consumes EC through an inner join on `sulfatefractions` and that table has no fuel-type-9 row.\n* NonECPM (118) -- 124 emitted, 0 of 104 right, off by 0.93 to 1.19. MOVES emits the RE-SUMMED 118 -- sulfate + water + a residue carrying the SAME base-rate fuel ratio on 12001 -- and the chain emits the rated one. The same 20 electricity rows.\n* SULFATE (115) AND WATER (119) -- FIXED AS A WRONG ANSWER, NOW ABSENT. The crankcase lift used to claim them through ratio-1 `crankcaseEmissionRatio` rows that are a row filter inside `SulfatePMCalculator`: sulfate came out as ALL of NonECPM, 1.7x to 68x high, and water as NonECPM where MOVES has 0.0. `rt_isSulfatePMSpecies` now keeps the lift off them, derived from the table (conventions 75), and `process-crankcase-running` is unchanged to the digit.\n* PM2.5 (110), OC (111) and PM10 (100) -- absent. `rt_pm10ChainRatio` already reads 1.13043 on 10001; its parent 11001 is what is missing.\n\nTHE ARITHMETIC, CONFIRMED FROM THE REFERENCE BEFORE ANY PORT. PM10 = PM2.5 x `PM10PM25Ratio` (1.13043, 1.08696 on diesel); 118-out = 115 + 119 + residue to 1e-5; OC = residue x `pmSpeciationFraction` (0.70672, 0.72582, 0.74170); and the sulfate fraction `SulfatenonECPMFraction x (1 + BaseFuelSulfateFraction x (sulfur/BaseFuelSulfurLevel - 1))` gives 0.027248, 0.066530 and 0.014773 by hand, equal to the fixture's own `rt_sulfateFraction`. What is NEW for the model is an operation and not data: a FRACTIONAL SPLIT of one parent into three siblings, one of them (120) internal and never emitted, and a RE-SUM back into the parent.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "process-pm-exhaust",
      "pm",
      "sulfate",
      "chained",
      "cyclic-declaration"
    ]
  },
